{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What person, known for their involvement in the civil rights movement, said the following: In the end, we will remember not the words of our enemies, but the silence of our friends.?","Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This conservationist, who along with his good friend Robert U. Johnson got Congress to approve a bill that would lead to the founding of Yosemite Sequoia National Parks, is remembered for the following quote: When one tugs at a single thing in nature, he finds it attached to the rest of the world.","John Muir"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What female writer, known for her very personal writings, said: And the day came when the risk to remain tight in a bud was more painful than the risk it took to blossom.?","Anaïs Nin"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This quote is from a coach that was so successful in his field that they named the champions trophy after him: We didnt lose the game; we just ran out of time.","Vince Lombardi"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The political figure who said Sometimes it is not enough to do our best; we must do what is required. was voted number one in the 2002 BBC poll of Greatest Britons Ever.","Sir Winston Churchill"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The woman who authored Coming of Age in Samoa also authored this quote: Never doubt that a small group of thoughtful committed citizens can change the world; indeed, its the only thing that ever has.","Margaret Mead"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This British author wrote about such issues as betrayal, murder and love; he also gave us the quote Ill deeds are doubled with an evil word.","William Shakespeare"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The controversial figure who gave us the following quote died of meningitis and is buried in the famed Pere Lachaise Cemetery in Paris. There are only two kinds of people who are really fascinating: people who know absolutely everything, and people who know absolutely nothing.","Oscar Wilde"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This German philosopher is the author of the book The Antichrist and also of this popular quote: You need chaos in your soul to give birth to a dancing star.","Friedrich Nietzsche"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["In 1998 we lost one of our greatest track and field competitors. Many people feel that she used steroids and that led to her early death.","Florence Griffith-Joyner"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Football star Derrick Thomas died in a shoot out outside a Kansas City club in 2000.","False"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What do Hugh OConnor and Cleopatra VII have in common?","They both committed suicide."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["In 1963 Patsy Cline killed her abusive husband and then turned the gun on herself.","False"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This famous writer, author of Les Miserables, wrote the following words: ...You have been privileged to receive every gift from nature, you have both fortitude and tears. Oh, Adele, do not mistake these words for blind enthusiasm - enthusiasm for you has lasted all my life, and increased day by day. My whole soul is yours. If my entire existence had not been yours, the harmony of my being would have been lost, and I must have died -- died inevitably.","Victor Hugo"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which famous person addressed the following words to his wife Clementine: Time passes swiftly, but is it not joyous to see how great and growing is the treasure we have gathered together, amid the storms and stresses of so many eventful and to millions tragic and terrible years??","Winston Churchill"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which famous poet wrote the following to his beloved Fanny Brawne: I cannot exist without you - I am forgetful of every thing but seeing you again - my life seems to stop there - I see no further. You have absorbd me.?","John Keats"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Name the politician who wrote the following words: Beware, Josephine; one fine night the doors will be broken down and there I shall be. In truth, I am worried, my love, to have no news from you; write me a four page letter instantly made up from those delightful words which fill my heart with emotion and joy.","Napoleon Bonaparte"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which New Zealand-born author wrote the following: Do not imagine, because you find these lines in your journal that I have been trespassing. You know I have not - and where else shall I leave a love letter? For I long to write you a love-letter tonight.?","Katherine Mansfield"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which US President addressed these words to his wife: ...Still this is the day, the day that marks 31 years of such happiness that has come to few me. I told you once that this was like adolescents dream of what marriage should be like. That hasnt changed.?","Ronald Reagan"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["With the following words, this famous person describes to his brother Theo the passion he feels for his cousin Kee: Life has become very dear to me, and I am very glad that I love. My life and my love are one. But you are faced with a no, never never is your reply. My answer to that is, Old boy, for the present I look upon that no, never never as a block of ice which I press to my heart to thaw.","Vincent Van Gogh"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Which writer and philosopher wrote the following while he was in prison: I am a prisoner here in the name of the King; they can take my life, but not the love that I feel for you. Yes, my adorable mistress, to-night I shall see you, and if I had to put my head on the block to do it.?","Voltaire"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["My father was also Commander in Chief. I served only one term as President. Who am I?","John Quincy Adams"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"people\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
